WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.110
Michael Murphy is probably best known for
playing the mayor in Batman Returns, but that's

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.750
not the only time he played an authority figure
in a superhero movie.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.420
Nor is it the only time that Paul Reubens
has played the father of a certain villain.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:18.289
We'd be willing to wager most folks already
know what Michael Keaton looks like today,

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:23.130
as he still appears in movies and TV shows
on a regular basis, even though he turned

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.300
70 in 2021.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:31.770
He had lead roles in back-to-back Best Picture
Oscar winners, 2014's Birdman and 2015's Spotlight.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:36.530
A few years later, he then had a small pivotal
part in the Aaron Sorkin-directed The Trial

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.070
of the Chicago 7.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.750
He then showed up on the Hulu miniseries Dopesick,
for which he won a Screen Actors Guild award

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.530
for Outstanding Male Actor in a TV Movie or
Miniseries.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.790
Keaton focuses a tad more on dramatic roles
these days, but if you thought he was done

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:56.140
with superheroes after he passed on 1995's
Batman Forever, you'd be highly mistaken.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:01.250
In an ironic nod to his time as the Dark Knight,
he played the Vulture, another winged comic

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.500
book icon, in 2017's Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.000
And he's even reportedly slated to reclaim
the cape and cowl and become Batman once again

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.930
in 2022's The Flash and HBO Max's Batgirl.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.939
Michelle Pfeiffer's A-lister status has hardly
diminished since the early 90s.

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:23.770
Her notable recent projects include the 2017
horror parable mother!, as well as the ensemble

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.180
crime caper Murder on the Orient Express,
also released in 2017.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:33.110
And then her performance in 2020's French
Exit garnered her a Golden Globe nomination.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:38.240
And as is the case with Michael Keaton, as
well as so many other actors working today,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.200
Pfeiffer is no stranger to the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.210
She made her first appearance as Janet Van
Dyne, the original Wasp, in 2019's Ant-Man

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:51.479
and the Wasp, and she's been confirmed to
reprise the role in 2023's Ant-Man and the

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:52.880
Wasp: Quantumania.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.130
And while several other actors have played
Selina Kyle in various projects over the years,

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.930
none have managed to convey anything like
the righteous mania of Pfeiffer's version.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:01.960
"Three lives down!

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.060
You got enough in there to finish me off?"

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:10.770
These days, Danny DeVito is most widely recognized
for playing a nihilistic crime lord with megalomaniacal

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.770
ambitions.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.640
We're speaking, of course, about disgraced
businessman Frank Reynolds on the long-running

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.420
sitcom It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.640
Like the version of the Penguin that DeVito
played in Batman Returns, Frank has virtually

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.520
zero capacity for ethics and morals.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:31.150
He's a pathological liar, a lech, a manipulator,
an embezzler, and an irresponsible gun owner.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.360
However, Frank also has something resembling
a heart that occasionally guides him towards

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.360
altruism.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.610
Nothing we see in Batman Returns, however,
leads us to believe that Oswald Cobblepot

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.900
is capable of any empathy at all.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.430
Then again, DeVito's Penguin never gets to
run a bar with his lovable slimeball buddies.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:51.610
If Oswald had the same second chance that
Frank has enjoyed, he'd probably still be

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.570
evil, but somewhat less evil.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:57.750
DeVito's career includes plenty of other highlights
in addition to those iconic characters.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:02.610
He was a regular on the 70s sitcom Taxi, and
he's starred in such varied movies as The

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:06.650
Jewel of the Nile, L.A. Confidential, and
Jumanji: The Next Level.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.420
He's also an accomplished behind-the-scenes
operator, having directed 1992's Hoffa and

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.650
2002's criminally underrated Death to Smoochy.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.210
Following his performance as diabolical capitalist
Max Shreck in Batman Returns, Christopher

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:26.130
Walken contributed his acting prowess to 1993's
True Romance and 1994's Pulp Fiction.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:32.950
He'll turn 80 in 2023, so it's perhaps unrealistic
to expect him to continue to crank out classics

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.050
at the same clip that he used to.

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:38.410
Regardless, his schedule doesn't seem to have
slowed down all that much.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:44.480
In 2022 alone, he co-stars in the BBC One
series The Outlaws, as well as the Apple TV+

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.730
thriller Severance.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:51.200
Walken has also shown up in a few clunkers
that predated this recent shift to TV, including

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:57.180
the 2020 family comedy The War with Grandpa,
as well as 2019's The Jesus Rolls, which featured

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.210
John Turturro's return to his minor character
from The Big Lebowski.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:05.840
On the positive side, Walken received considerable
praise for his performance as a humble farmer

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:11.830
in 2020's Percy Vs. Goliath, a considerable
turn against type, considering how closely

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:16.139
he's been associated with villainous roles
throughout his career.

00:04:16.139 --> 00:04:20.320
"Bruce Wayne, why are you dressed up like
Batman?"

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.900
Thanks to Pee-wee's Big Adventure in 1985
and owning Saturday morning kids TV from 1986

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:31.340
to 1990 with Pee-wee's Playhouse, Paul Reubens
was already a certified household name by

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:35.060
the time of Batman Returns' release in 1992.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:39.560
Decades later, he brought his alter ego back
for one more go-round in 2016's Pee-wee's

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:40.560
Big Holiday.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.400
But besides that, this comedy legend has revisited
his signature character relatively infrequently

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.560
since the 80s.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.560
"Pee-wee!"

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.400
"That's my name, don't wear it out."

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.911
Nowadays, Reubens tends to show up here and
there in various films and TV shows, having

00:04:54.911 --> 00:04:59.750
lately contributed cameos to the ABC game
show To Tell the Truth and the FX vampire

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.080
mockumentary What We Do in the Shadows.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.510
Astoundingly enough, Reubens' performance
as the Penguin's criminally negligent father

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:11.430
in Batman Returns is much smaller than his
other Batman-related roles, at least in terms

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.810
of minutes onscreen.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:18.470
He provided the voice of Bat-Mite in multiple
episodes of the 2009 animated series Batman:

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:22.500
The Brave and the Bold, and he played a much
more sympathetic version of the Penguin's

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:27.300
dad for an arc on Fox's Batman prequel series
Gotham.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.380
Casting Diane Salinger and Paul Reubens as
the Penguin's parents was a clear tribute

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.290
to Tim Burton's directorial debut, Pee-wee's
Big Adventure.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:39.970
In that earlier feature, Salinger played Simone,
an adventurous woman who's trapped in a loveless

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.440
marriage and a dead-end waitressing job.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.830
While Salinger's hardly the biggest name from
Batman Returns, she has enjoyed a consistent

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.810
and interesting presence in film and TV since
the mid-80s.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:56.341
This has included stints on HBO's mid-2000s
Dust Bowl apocalypse drama Carnivàle and

00:05:56.341 --> 00:06:02.200
2000's Power Rangers Lightspeed Rescue, for
which she provided the voice of Queen Bansheera.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:07.190
Salinger also played a therapist in the 2001
cult comedy Ghost World, which means that

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.290
even if she never gets her own Marvel franchise,
she's still the only actor on this list who

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:16.020
had a scene with Steve Buscemi in Thora Birch's
best movie.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.250
Arguably underutilized in Batman Returns,
Michael Murphy's character doesn't even have

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.380
an actual name listed on the film's IMDb page.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.420
Instead, he's simply known as "Mayor."

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.630
Although, he can at least rest assured that
the novelization of the film reportedly does

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:31.990
name this character as "Roscoe Jenkins."

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.920
As for Murphy himself, he hasn't slowed down
as much as you might expect for someone in

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:36.920
his 80s.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:43.430
He appears in Netflix's 2019 Bob Dylan documentary
Rolling Thunder Revue, and he's provided voiceovers

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:48.810
for episodes of PBS's American Experience
as recently as 2020.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:53.280
Having started his film and TV career in the
early 60s, there's a lot more to Murphy than

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.110
a medium-sized part in a Caped Crusader flick.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:07:00.530
He's known for his several collaborations
with director Robert Altman, and Batman Returns

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:05.260
isn't even his only significant superhero
movie, as he played Warren Worthington III's

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:09.070
dad in 2006's X-Men: The Last Stand.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:14.120
Former Saturday Night Live staple Jan Hooks
briefly pops up in Batman Returns as Jen,

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.580
one of Max Shreck's personal image consultants.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:22.500
In addition to her SNL tenure from 1986 to
1991, her TV credits include the likes of

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.400
Designing Women, 3rd Rock from the Sun, and
Primetime Glick.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.720
She passed away in 2014 at the age of 57,
and some present-day showbiz movers and shakers

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.060
think she was owed a little more applause
during her time on Earth.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:39.560
During Elle's Women in Hollywood Awards in
2014, Tina Fey profanely declared,

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.640
"Jan should have had a bigger career.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.920
Jan deserved a big movie career.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.390
Certainly as big as Rob Schneider's f---ing
career.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.870
She was a bigger star on SNL."

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.360
We're not saying Tina Fey is right all of
the time; even though she's plenty smart and

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.240
funny, nobody is right 100 percent of the
time.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:59.400
But we can say objectively and definitively
that when it comes to Jan Hooks, Tina Fey

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.960
is unequivocally correct.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:06.230
If you ask us, having his nose nearly bitten
off by the Penguin during an ill-advised image

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:10.130
consultation session is the zenith of Steve
Witting's career.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:14.250
But it's hardly his only on-screen highlight,
as he's been a regular player in the background

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.889
of major film and TV endeavors since the mid-80s.

00:08:17.889 --> 00:08:22.110
He's certainly been doing pretty okay in the
last decade or so, especially when it comes

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:27.490
to movies directed by Martin Scorsese, as
he showed up in 2010's Shutter Island, 2013's

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:31.389
The Wolf of Wall Street and 2019's The Irishman.

00:08:31.389 --> 00:08:35.830
And he's booked a role in Scorsese's upcoming
western Killers of the Flower Moon.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:40.500
Witting has additionally appeared in a handful
of this era's most significant TV shows, including

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:46.240
It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia and Arrested
Development, and he also showed up in the

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.980
2020 HBO miniseries The Outsider.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:53.690
And Batman Returns wasn't his only collaboration
in 1992 with Danny DeVito, as he showed up

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:58.520
in the DeVito-helmed Hoffa, in which Jack
Nicholson plays the infamous labor organizer

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.850
who gave the film its name.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.560
Most of the actors on this list don't appear
in all four entries of the series that begins

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.570
with 1989's Batman and ends with 1997's Batman
and Robin.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:13.370
But the tenacious Michael Gough is Bruce Wayne's
loyal butler Alfred Pennyworth throughout

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.370
the saga.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:19.270
The latter two films, Batman and Robin and
1995's Batman Forever, aren't exactly the

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:22.960
most acclaimed entries in the Caped Crusader's
onscreen saga.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.090
But even if some of the movies that feature
Gough aren't that good, we doubt that Christopher

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:31.110
Nolan would've made sure to hire someone on
the level of Michael Caine to play a new Alfred

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:36.290
in 2005's Batman Begins if Gough's portrayal
weren't a very tough act to follow.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:39.690
Gough passed away in 2011 at the age of 94.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:45.150
His onscreen career began in the 1940s, and
he kept acting regularly throughout the 90s,

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.860
with a handful of parts after the year 2000.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.780
Despite his appearances in high-profile films
like Out of Africa and The Boys from Brazil,

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:56.430
his obituaries understandably tended to focus
on his run as Alfred.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.430
"Ready?"

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:00.170
"I think I'll take the stairs."

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:04.460
Commissioner James Gordon didn't have a ton
to do during this particular era of Batman

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:05.460
movies.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.850
This version of Gordon, played by veteran
character actor Pat Hingle, has much more

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:13.520
in common with the noble bumbler portrayed
by Neil Hamilton in the campy 60s Batman TV

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:18.570
show than with the determined everyman channeled
by Gary Oldman in Christopher Nolan's Batman

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:19.570
trilogy.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:23.450
Oddly enough, the timing of Hingle's life
and career make us wonder why he wasn't cast

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.140
in the 60s Batman.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:29.730
During that era, he routinely made guest appearances
on such iconic series as Mission: Impossible

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.690
and The Andy Griffith Show.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:37.430
IMDb lists the ridiculously prolific Hingle's
first credit as a 1951 episode of Suspense

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:42.850
and his final credit as a 2008 film called
Undoing Time, with very little downtime in

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:43.850
between.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.460
He died in 2009 at the age of 84.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:50.870
Despite having played literally dozens of
other parts, the headlines of Hingle's obituaries

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:54.120
largely emphasized his Batman-related work.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:58.710
Ironically, the nameless "Organ Grinder" in
Batman Returns is played by one of the most

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.870
recognizable actors in the film.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:06.120
Noted for his unusual facial features, Vincent
Schiavelli arrived on plenty of people's radar

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:11.779
with his performance as a mental institution
patient in the 1975 classic One Flew Over

00:11:11.779 --> 00:11:12.779
The Cuckoo's Nest.

00:11:12.779 --> 00:11:17.300
As fate would have it, Cuckoo's Nest also
marked a career milestone for fellow future

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.910
Batman villains Jack Nicholson and Danny DeVito.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:25.230
After Cuckoo's Nest, Hollywood tapped Schiavelli
pretty much whenever a distinctively odd but

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.790
non-threatening presence was required.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:34.210
This included parts in the likes of 1982's
Fast Times at Ridgemont High, 1990's Ghost,

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.410
and 1997's Tomorrow Never Dies.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:41.540
Additionally, Schiavelli made guest appearances
on so many significant TV series that we don't

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.690
even know how to start listing them.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:48.990
But if we have to pick one, let's go with
Lanny the conjoined twin from the 1995 X-Files

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.620
episode "Humbug."

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:54.810
Schiavelli passed away in 2005 at the age
of 57.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:58.300
"Get off my train!"

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.570
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:05.490
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and TV shows are coming soon.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:09.700
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

